  "question_stem": "A particle $P$ of mass $6\\text{ kg}$ lies on a rough plane inclined at an acute angle $\\theta$ to the horizontal. A horizontal force of magnitude $12\\text{ N}$ acts on $P$ as shown in the diagram. The line of action of this horizontal force lies in a vertical plane which contains the line of greatest slope of the plane that passes through $P$. The coefficient of friction between $P$ and the plane is $\\mu$.\n\n$P$ is in equilibrium and on the point of sliding down the plane.",
  "context_texts": [
    "$\\mu=\\dfrac{5\\tan\\theta-1}{5+\\tan\\theta}$"
  ],
